    "intro_html":  "Bobotie is South Africa\u0027s national dish and it is stranger and better than it sounds. Curried ground beef gets sweetened with raisins and honey, sharpened with vinegar, bound with milk-soaked bread, and then a savory egg custard is poured over the top and baked until it sets like a golden lid. Sweet, sour, spiced, and creamy all at once. It has been made in the Cape for centuries, and it happens to be perfectly suited to a big dish and fourteen containers.",
